# Phase discipline

Read [docs/master-spec.md](docs/master-spec.md) and the current phase doc before changing code.

Work only on the current phase. The current phase is Phase 1. See [docs/phase-1.md](docs/phase-1.md).

Feature work happens on `develop`. Merge to `main` only when the user is ready for production.

Phase 1 is pipeline proof only: static homepage, `system_health` migration, GitHub Actions, Vercel. Do not add Bybit, the opportunity scanner, auth, encrypted exchange keys, or an execution engine.

Do not create later-phase tables or speculative architecture.

Keep dependencies minimal. Prefer the simplest solution that satisfies the current phase.

Work one micro-step at a time as listed in [docs/phase-1.md](docs/phase-1.md). Stop at the end of each micro-step and wait for instruction.

Stop at the end of the phase. After acceptance criteria pass, report results and wait for instruction.
